    <string name="feature_packages_why_title">Why official packages do not work</string>
    <string name="feature_packages_why_explanation">Termux packages embed the app’s private prefix. Official packages use /data/data/com.termux, while Termux RE can access /data/data/com.termux.re. A package built for the official app may therefore install but fail to find its shell, libraries, configuration or data.</string>
    <string name="feature_packages_options_title">What you can do</string>
    <string name="feature_packages_options_explanation">Request a Termux RE build using the package-request form, or install the official Termux app separately when you need its full package catalog. Do not mix incompatible .deb files into this environment.</string>
    <string name="feature_packages_get_official">Get official Termux</string>
    <string name="feature_packages_check_title">Compatibility checker</string>
    <string name="feature_packages_check_explanation">Scan installed package file lists or a local .deb for /data/data/com.termux paths that do not use the Termux RE prefix. This detects a common incompatibility; a clean scan does not guarantee that a package will work.</string>
